    "created_at": "2016-07-19T17:32:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-19T17:32:43Z",
    "body": "(I also put my comment in PR, will paraphrase it here.)\n\nCSS agrees with this practice - we very intentionally only have two modes for handling text, depending on context: either the context is ASCII-only, in which case we compare case-insensitively, or the context is full Unicode, in which case we compare codepoint-wise.  No normalization ever occurs, and we specifically intend to never do normalization.  If multiple authors on a single project are outputting differently-normalized text, that's an error on their side, and not one we're going to work around.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
